"Apply for a Texas Driver License | Department of Public Safety (https://www.dps.texas.gov/section/driver-license/how-apply-texas-driver-license)\nciteturn24view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.dps.texas.gov/section/driver-license/how-apply-texas-driver-license\",\"lineno\":null}); Redirected to URL: https://www.dps.texas.gov/section/driver-license/apply-texas-driver-license; Total lines: 69\nL0: Search Form Search\nL1: \nL2: [Input: What can we help you find?]\nL3: \nL4: [Button: Search]\nL5: \nL6: [Input] [Input]\nL7: \nL8: ## Change Text Size\nL9: \nL10: ^{-}A A ^{+}A\nL11: \nL12: ## Change Display Setting\nL13: \nL14: cite0†Default cite1†Text Only L15: # Apply for a Texas Driver License\nL16: \nL17: November 25, 2024\nL18: \nL19: Before your driver license appointment, use the cite2†REAL ID Document Check tool.  This quick online tool asks you questions and creates a personalized list of exactly what documents you will need.\nL20: \nL21: Use resources like the cite3†Texas Driver’s Handbook and cite4†\"What it takes to Apply for a DL or ID Card\" brochure for more information.\nL22: \nL23: If you already have a Texas ID, you will need to surrender it when you get you apply for a driver license.\nL24: Step 1.  Gather the Required Documentation:\nL25:   1. Proof of cite5†U.S. Citizenship or Lcite5†awful Presence (if not a U.S. Citizen)\nL26:   2. Proof of cite6†Texas Residency L27:   3. Proof of cite7†Identity L28:   4. Social Security Number\nL29:   5. Evidence of current Texas Vehicle Registration for each vehicle you own. Visit cite8†Texas Vehicle Registration†renew.txdmv.gov website for more information.  Proof of vehicle registration applies to new residents who are surrendering an out-of-state driver license only.\nL30:   6. Proof of Insurance for each vehicle you own or a statement affirming you do not own a vehicle.\nL31:   7. cite9†Impact Texas Driver (ITD) certificate, if you will be taking a driving test for the issuance of your driver license.  The certificate must be dated within 90 days for your driving skills test.\nL32:   8. A six-hour adult cite10†Driver Education†www.tdlr.texas.gov course, if you are 18 through 24 years of age and applying for your first Texas driver license.  This requirement is waived for new residents 18 or older who are surrendering a valid, unexpired driver license from another state.  (No driver education requirements for ages 25 and older)\nL33: Step 2.  Visit a Driver License Office:\nL34:   1. Visit cite11†Driver License Services – Appointments to schedule an appointment at your local driver license office.\nL35:   2. Complete the cite12†application , available online or at the office.\nL36:   3. Provide the following documentation to the license and permit specialist:\nL37:     1. Completed driver license cite12†Application form\nL38:     2. Proof of cite5†U.S. Citizenship or Lcite5†awful Presence (if not a U.S. Citizen)\nL39:     3. Proof of cite6†Texas Residency , and\nL40:     4. Proof of cite7†Identity .\nL41:   4. Provide Biometric Information (signature and thumbprints)\nL42:   5. Have your picture taken.\nL43:   6. Pay the application cite13†fee .\nL44:   7. Pass the vision exam.\nL45:   8. Pass the written knowledge and a practical cite14†driving skills test to demonstrate your understanding of traffic laws and safe driving practices. You may complete the testing requirements at the DPS office or with a cite15†Third Party provider .\nL46: Step 3.  The Final Steps:\nL47: \nL48: Once your driver license has been issued, you will receive a temporary driver license that allows you to drive legally while you wait for your permanent card.\nL49:   * Before leaving the driver license office, carefully review the printed information on your temporary driver license for accuracy.  If any of the information is incorrect, please notify the license and permit specialist.\nL50:   * Your official driver license will typically arrive by mail within 2-3 weeks.  To check the mailing status of your card, visit our cite16†mailing status web page.\nL51: \nL52: The following applicants may have additional requirements or services available.  Select below for more information:\nL53: cite17†New Texas Residents L54: \nL55: cite18†Teen Drivers Applicants (Under 18 years old) L56: \nL57: cite5†Temporary Visitors and Foreign Students L58: \nL59: cite19†Motorcycle Applicants L60: \nL61: cite20†Veteran Services L62: ### Follow DPS\nL63: \nL64: ### Keep Texas Safe\nL65: \nL66: cite21†Report Suspicious Activity†iwatchtx.org L67: \nL68: © 2026 Texas Department of Public Safety. PDF files require cite22†Adobe Reader†get.adobe.com or compatible.\n"
